      {
        "id": 227341,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-05-06T17:52:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, the core game Blight cards are just awful.&nbsp; I also recommend trying out the more complex spirits first, so you can learn to appreciate them and pick your favorites.</p>\n<p>As for Blight card vs. Adversaries... Adversaries are probably more fun, as you get to experience different strategies, and actually make use of the Stage II escalation effects.&nbsp; Blight cards are mandatory with later expansion content, but the Blight cards than come with them are substantially easier to deal with.</p>\n<p>On the other hand, it's good to practice with Blight cards sooner rather than later, because you can easily get spoiled with having such a large Blight pool.&nbsp; You may want to split your Blight pool in two: one with 2/player, one with 3/player, and try to avoid emptying the first pool as long as possible.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:01:30.831Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
